WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:03.660
(playful piano music)

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:07.340
- [Woman] Deep in the bayou,
on this street, down this road,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.210
in this windowless tin
shack, is a restaurant

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.230
run by one woman, whose
dishes are so good,

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.660
you have to wait a year to try them.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.830
- I'm Alzina Toups and I've
been cooking Cajun food

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.496
for at least over 60 years.

00:00:21.496 --> 00:00:24.663
(playful piano music)

00:00:26.231 --> 00:00:29.510
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.130
- [Woman] Welcome to Alazina's.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.010
A Cajun restaurant with
no staff and no menu.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.120
Just Chef Alzina and her kitchen.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.080
And it's housed in one of
the most unassuming places.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.233
A former welding shop that
was once owned by her son.

00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:46.700
- I turned this into kitchen
because I loved cooking.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.273
And you don't have that
big bump in the middle.

00:00:49.273 --> 00:00:50.360
- Right.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.300
- My son was in the process
of moving to a bigger place

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.350
so instead of closing it,

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.550
he asked me if I wanted to convert this.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.490
So I converted into a kitchen.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.070
I wanted to be open.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:05.820
Where I cook and where they eat.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.100
Because they can see what you're doing.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.600
Most of the people that come,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.500
they want to take part in what you do.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.860
Cajun food I think is the
best food in the world.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.330
I was raised on it.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.630
To me it's simple cooking.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.730
You start with your bell pepper.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:26.290
You have onion, you have
garlic, a lot of garlic,

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:31.170
celery, and then you saute
that in a small amount of oil.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.900
And then you start adding
your other ingredients.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.740
Whatever you're cooking, if
it's a gumbo or jambalaya

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.536
or fried shrimp, what's better than that?

00:01:39.536 --> 00:01:42.480
(playful instrumental music)

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:43.850
- [Woman] As good as that sounds,

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.980
eating at Alzina's can be tricky.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.100
There are no walk-ins and reservations

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:51.160
can only be made by calling
her on her landline phone.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.420
- Thank you for calling.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.960
I didn't want walk-in because I think

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.230
I would have been very unhappy.

00:01:57.230 --> 00:02:01.080
I live a simple life and this
is the way I like my life.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.000
Simple.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.040
No computer, just a simple telephone.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.700
I'm booked up until next year.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.640
I'm always booked up in a year advance.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.773
And I like it better that way.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.870
- [Woman] Over those 40
years, Alzina's has been

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.880
pretty successful garnering
the attention of magazines,

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.170
politicians and celebrity chefs.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:24.340
People from all over
the world have flocked

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.410
to Alzina's kitchen for
her authentic Cajun food.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.210
But for Alzina, the experience

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.388
is all about making people feel at home.

00:02:31.388 --> 00:02:33.040
Like a family.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.970
- When people come, it's a tin building.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:38.734
So they see where we're
at and you don't realize

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.361
that it's here.

00:02:40.361 --> 00:02:42.870
But when they step in the kitchen,

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.550
it's a different world.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.120
I really think they're happy.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.893
I feel the peace in the
kitchen and then they mingle,

00:02:50.893 --> 00:02:54.150
family that haven't seen
each other for maybe a year,

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.450
two, three years.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.330
It bring happiness to them.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.849
And it bring happiness to me.

00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:03.652
I was born to serve, not to be served.

00:03:03.652 --> 00:03:06.819
(playful piano music)

